{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411922-homebrewing-charms-how-to-make-ability-based-charm-trees-work","id":1411922,"title":"Homebrewing charms - how to make ability-based charm trees work?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-04T16:15:32-07:00","id":1411922,"title":"Homebrewing charms - how to make ability-based charm trees work?","content":"(EDITING because there was some term confusion, hope it works now)<br /> <br /> Some time ago I made an attempt to write some charm trees for liminals. Someone told me they should be attribute-based rather than ability based (makes sense. What kind of a charm tree would a liminal have for sailing ?)<br /> <br /> But trying to do that is tricky, because some abilities span multiple attributes, so charms that would normally for a coherent whole end up in different trees. Has any of you tried that before? What is your advice for making it work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23788,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","user":"Braininthejar","date":". 09-04-2020, 08:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T16:48:25-07:00","id":1411932,"title":"","content":"One thing to remember when designing Ability charms is that the Abilities aren't necessarily totally exclusive in the tasks they allow people to do. Take navigating, for example - by default, it's a Survival roll. But someone with Sail can also navigate across the sea. And no matter which Ability you've got, those techniques aren't suddenly going to get forgotten when you're not in the wilderness or not standing on the deck of a ship. Someone with Survival can use it to navigate while they're sailing a ship, and someone with Sail can use it to navigate while trekking on foot through the desert (there might be penalties for unfamiliarity or lack of appropriate tools, though). So, while most Abilities can't necessarily do <i>everything </i>associated with a particular archetype (someone with Sail can't use it to make a good bargain for their next cargo, or swing a cutlass, or build a whole boat), it <i>is</i> all right to let charms in that Ability do stuff that other Abilities would also cover, as long as doing that thing is a central feature of that Ability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T17:21:26-07:00","id":1411947,"title":"","content":"So... I should construct charms in a way that gives some flexibility to what skills they can be used for, while creating some general themes for each ability?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T17:35:06-07:00","id":1411955,"title":"","content":"What exactly do you mean by &quot;skills&quot;? A clearer explanation of that might help us help you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T17:35:29-07:00","id":1411956,"title":"","content":"Just a nitpick: You mean attribute based, not ability based.<br /> Ability is what we formally call what you called skills. Strength, Intelligence, Charisma...these are attributes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T17:40:04-07:00","id":1411959,"title":"","content":"Part of the confusion here is that in the old World of Darkness and in Exalted you had Attributes, which are the things like Strength and Dexterity and Intelligence, and then you have Abilities, which are things like Ride and Melee. (In the oWoD, Abilities were divided into Talents, Skills, and Knowledges)<br /> <br /> But in the Chronicles of Darkness, there's Attributes and Skills, not Attributes and Abilities.<br /> <br /> ...<i>but in D&amp;D</i>, which is where a lot of people enter the hobby and learn the core terminology, Strength, Dexterity, Constitution, Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma <i>are called Ability Scores</i>, and the word &quot;Attributes&quot; is not used.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T17:42:39-07:00","id":1411961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411922-homebrewing-charms-how-to-make-ability-based-charm-trees-work?p=1411956#post1411956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a nitpick: You mean attribute based, not ability based.<br /> Ability is what we formally call what you called skills. Strength, Intelligence, Charisma...these are attributes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. I'm used to thinking about the game in Polish, and when writing in English I sometimes translate stuff without thinking. <br /> <br /> Yes. I mean things like &quot;some of the stuff done with brawl would land under strength, some under dexterity and some under endurance. I could probably put social actions under manipulation but they'd need intelligence to be done in writing&quot; and so on.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T17:42:39-07:00","id":1411962,"title":"","content":"Edit: also, my mouse is broken, and sometimes a click results in double or triple clicking - but how does the forum makes double posts out of it, I don't understand...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T17:43:42-07:00","id":1411963,"title":"","content":"No big. Just edit the title and first post to facilitate it for the next readers and you should be set!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T18:07:25-07:00","id":1411966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411922-homebrewing-charms-how-to-make-ability-based-charm-trees-work?p=1411963#post1411963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No big. Just edit the title and first post to facilitate it for the next readers and you should be set!</div> </div> </div> </div>doesn't let me change the title for some reason. changes the description though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ok, trying to see how it would work...<br /> <br /> STRENGTH: strength-based athletics, boosting close combat damage<br /> DEXTERITY: agility-based athletics, boosting dodge and close combat attacks, creepy contortionist tricks, manipulating blood (turning semi-liquid?) <br /> ENDURANCE: self repair, increasing soak, creating dummy health levels, creating tools, weapons and armor out of transformed bone.<br /> <br /> CHARISMA: intimidation, repelling and cowing ghosts and undead. (wounding spirits?)<br /> MANIPULATION: messing with people's emotions, messing with people's internal chemistry.<br /> APPEARANCE: self-inflicted plastic surgery, wearing people as disguises, switching 'hideous' on and off.<br /> <br /> PERCEPTION: seeing in the dark, seeing spirits, postcognition and psychometry powers?<br /> INTELLIGENCE: occult and craft related powers, borrowing memories from the dead to boost abilities. Also crafting? Crossing into the realm of the dead?<br /> WITS: sensing impending danger, giving people bad luck. <br /> <br /> It seems there are following things I need to adress:<br /> <br /> 1 Some attributes, have a lot more stuff than others. I need something more for wits and appearance, and perhaps to move some stuff out of dexterity and endurance, but what?<br /> 2 I still haven't got a place for decay-based charms, and for storing away weapons (something all exalts have in some form) <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T18:19:28-07:00","id":1411968,"title":"","content":"strength could have powers that give and take strength to others, too. You take body parts the moment you chop them off your enemies, gaining some sort of strength in the process. Maybe give them to a friend as a very icky buff.<br /> <br /> Wits might include crazy usage of body parts. Cancel a crippling attack's effect because it chopped off the body part but in whatever form it attached itself works fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T18:29:56-07:00","id":1411969,"title":"","content":"Hmm... the body manipulation things feel like they should be in physical attributes, and mostly in endurance...<br /> <br /> Perhaps wits could get entropic powers, - banking successes because you feel when things could go wrong, intuitively feel how things decay and speed it along.<br /> Perhaps grave themed powers - 'bury' your sword to pull out later bury yourself to sleep safely. move underground and through walls. try to pull a grappled foe into the ground. Or would that work better with a different atribute?<br /> <br /> What about making temporary zombies - not through necromancy (your boss hates that) but through directly puppeteering bodies with essence? where would that go?<br /> <br /> I still need some more ideas for appearance","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T18:44:58-07:00","id":1411973,"title":"","content":"3e Lunars have a full Attribute based charmset. What they do is they subdivide each attribute in multiple trees - for instance, Appearance has 3 trees: Influence, Subterfuge and Warfare, while Strength has the 3 trees Offense, Feats of Strength, and Mobility. You can look at <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/exalted/comments/b0e9t5/madletters_charm_cascades_lunar_solar/\" target=\"_blank\">Madletter's Charm Cascades</a> to get an overview of the Lunar Attribute Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T18:53:05-07:00","id":1411974,"title":"","content":"That's.... a lot of charms. I definitely need to come up with more stuff...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T19:56:07-07:00","id":1411991,"title":"","content":"Think less about quantity and more take a look at how Lunar Charms are divided between \u201cGoes with this one Ability\u201d and \u201cApplicable to several Abilities if not all the ones (Attribute) commonly goes with.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T06:50:21-07:00","id":1412069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1411922-homebrewing-charms-how-to-make-ability-based-charm-trees-work?p=1411973#post1411973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3e Lunars have a full Attribute based charmset. What they do is they subdivide each attribute in multiple trees - for instance, Appearance has 3 trees: Influence, Subterfuge and Warfare, while Strength has the 3 trees Offense, Feats of Strength, and Mobility. You can look at <a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/exalted/comments/b0e9t5/madletters_charm_cascades_lunar_solar/\" target=\"_blank\">Madletter's Charm Cascades</a> to get an overview of the Lunar Attribute Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, it would be something like...<br /> <br /> CHARISMA - EXORCISM<br /> <br /> E1<br /> * trace a trail of dust from fingertips, make it act like a line of salt<br /> * be able to touch/hit dematerialised spirits, as well as grapple magically elusive foes.<br /> * cut yourself, make the smell of your blood a lure for wraiths and hungry ghosts<br /> <br /> E2<br /> * roll charisma+occult on a ghost you hit, to force him to dematerialise (can be used to punch possessing spirits out of people)<br /> * make a ghost feel alive again, making it emotionally unstable and more susseptible to social influence.<br /> * convert E damage dealt to a spirit or undead into aggreviated.<br /> * disperse the anima in a burst of energy painful to the dead (a normal attack with an area effect, good against battle groups)<br /> * force all nearby undead to make disengage rolls.<br /> <br /> E3<br /> * grapple a ghost with a charisma+occult control roll. Spend 3 rounds of control on a special throw to yeet him to a corresponding location in Underworld.<br /> * once per day gain a willpower point from defeating a non-trivial dead.<br /> * roll a non-charm die when attacking the dead who are in initiative crash.<br /> <br /> E4<br /> * project bonfire anima as a sphere of energy that keeps burning nearby undead.<br /> * grapple a ghost - make painful savage attacks that try to break his will and force him into Lethe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23788,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","user":"Braininthejar","date":". 09-05-2020, 10:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23788-braininthejar","name":"Braininthejar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}